 in microstructure are empirical in nature, and we will spend time on the empirical approaches used in such research. We will discuss a variety of current market microstructure topics including high-frequency trading and OTC markets. Because information and liquidity issues are fundamental to many of the issues covered in microstructure, this course should be of interest to students in a wide range of disciplines.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GM", "acadGroup": "BU", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2811, "crseId": 364307, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "NRE", "catalogNbr": "5030", "titleShort": "App Microecon II: Game Theory", "titleLong": "Applied Microeconomics II: Game Theory", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 19892, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "08:40AM", "timeEnd": "09:55AM", "startDt": "01/24/2022", "endDt": "04/10/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "mw46", "firstName": "Michael", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Waldman"}], "pattern": "MW", "facilityDescr": "Sage Graduate Hall B09", "bldgDescr": "Sage Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "SGHB09", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}, {"classMtgNbr": 2, "timeStart": "08:40AM", "timeEnd": "09:55AM", "startDt": "04/11/2022", "endDt": "04/11/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "mw46", "firstName": "Michael", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Waldman"}], "pattern": "M", "facilityDescr": "Sage Graduate Hall B08", "bldgDescr": "Sage Hall", "